@startuml
title SA-F06 — Event settlement and closure
caption Event payment, service and equipment settlement | PRD-15–17
start
:Check quote is at least RM0.02 with both instalments positive;
:Review 50 percent deposit against the quote and its payment deadline;
if (Deposit has verified shortfall?) then (yes)
 if (Current cutoff still ahead?) then (yes)
  :Notify exact difference without changing cutoff;
  :Verify each transfer and settle only at exact eligible total;
 else (no)
  :Keep actual receipts and route to manual disposition;
 endif
endif
if (Verified and quote eligible?) then (yes)
 :Confirm booking and show balance deadline;
 if (Balance has verified shortfall?) then (yes)
  :Use the existing balance cutoff and verify each transfer;
  :Route any remaining shortfall after cutoff to manual disposition;
 endif
 if (Balance overdue?) then (yes)
  :Remind, allow 24-hour grace and route to merchant decision;
  if (Timely balance proof still under review at grace expiry?) then (yes)
   :Keep resources reserved while merchant reviews actual funds;
  endif
  :Allow nonpayment cancellation only after cutoff, resolved review and verified absence of balance funds;
 endif
 :Block customer cancellation after transfer and customer-initiated refund after balance payment;
 if (Booking proceeds?) then (yes)
  :Complete setup and teardown;
  :Check equipment, damage and waiting;
  if (Additional charge?) then (yes)
   :Itemize charge and reconcile separate payment;
  endif
 else (cancelled)
  :Release unused resources on authorized cancellation;
  :Refund all receipts if merchant cannot fulfil;
 endif
else (no)
 :Expire quote or send payment anomaly for reconciliation;
endif
if (Merchant and customer pursue reschedule?) then (yes)
 :Retain paid balance or recalculate outstanding due from new date minus three days and add 24 hours grace;
 if (New due cannot be met?) then (yes)
  :Agree another date or refund;
 endif
endif
stop
@enduml
